{"name":"Inland Waters","hex":"#7c939d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"inland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Within the land; relatively remote from the ocean or from open water; interior.","Limited to the land, or to inland routes; not passing on, or over, the sea."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The interior part of a country."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inland"},{"term":"waters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of water","Amniotic fluid ."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Internal waters","blocks":[{"text":"According to the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea, a nation's internal waters include waters on the side of the baseline of a nation's territorial waters that is facing toward the land, except in archipelagic states. It includes waterways such as rivers and canals, and sometimes the water within small bays."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Maritime_Zones_under_International_Law.png/330px-Maritime_Zones_under_International_Law.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internal_waters","wikidata":"Q1663988"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"inland":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/En-us-inland.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/20/En-us-inland.ogg/En-us-inland.ogg.mp3"}],"waters":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/En-us-waters.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/tr